---
// The workspace's packages and their dependencies, drawn from the manifests as the site builds,
// so the diagram is never out of date. Drawn with Starlight's colour variables so it follows the
// light and dark themes.
import { BOX_HEIGHT, BOX_WIDTH, dependencyGraph } from "./dependency-graph.ts";

const graph = dependencyGraph();
---

<figure class="dependencies">
  <div class="scroll">
    <svg
      viewBox={`0 0 ${graph.width.toFixed(0)} ${graph.height.toFixed(0)}`}
      style={`max-width: ${graph.width.toFixed(0)}px`}
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="dependencies-title dependencies-desc"
    >
      <title id="dependencies-title">Workspace package dependencies</title>
      <desc id="dependencies-desc">{graph.description}</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker
          id="dependencies-arrow"
          viewBox="0 0 10 10"
          refX="9"
          refY="5"
          markerWidth="7"
          markerHeight="7"
          orient="auto-start-reverse"
        >
          <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="head"></path>
        </marker>
      </defs>

      {
        graph.lines.map((line) => (
          <path class:list={["line", { dev: line.dev }]} d={line.path}>
            <title>{`${line.from} → ${line.to}`}</title>
          </path>
        ))
      }
      {
        graph.boxes.map((box) => (
          <g>
            <rect
              class:list={["box", { published: box.published }]}
              x={box.x.toFixed(1)}
              y={box.y.toFixed(1)}
              width={BOX_WIDTH}
              height={BOX_HEIGHT}
              rx="6"
            />
            <text class="name" x={(box.x + 12).toFixed(1)} y={(box.y + 20).toFixed(1)}>
              {box.name}
            </text>
            <text class="directory" x={(box.x + 12).toFixed(1)} y={(box.y + 36).toFixed(1)}>
              {box.directory}
            </text>
          </g>
        ))
      }
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    Each package sits above what it depends on. Every gateway is drawn as one box, and every
    driver as another, since each has the same shape. An arrow is left out where another
    dependency already reaches the package. A dashed arrow is a dev dependency only. A highlighted package is
    in the <code>@govuk-once/</code> scope. The shared ESLint, TypeScript and Vitest configuration,
    which every package uses, is left out, and so is this site.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .dependencies {
    margin-block: 1.5rem;
  }
  .scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 900px;
    height: auto;
    margin-inline: auto;
    font-family: var(--sl-font);
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .box {
    fill: var(--sl-color-bg);
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
  }
  .box.published {
    stroke: var(--sl-color-accent);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    marker-end: url(#dependencies-arrow);
  }
  .line.dev {
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }
  .head {
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
  text {
    fill: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  /* As Starlight resolves its own: --sl-font-mono is only set to override the system font. */
  .name,
  .directory {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono, var(--sl-font-system-mono));
  }
  .name {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .directory {
    font-size: 11px;
    fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
</style>
